<!-- 01 — THE SITUATION -->
<section class="container measure section-block section-block--tight">
  <p class="label reveal" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">01 — The situation</p>
  <h2 class="display-md reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom:1.25rem;">World market leader in a niche – and invisible</h2>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-2" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Many machine builders are technology or world market leaders in their segment. From the outside, this is often not nearly as visible as the company's technical importance would justify. The brand presence still shows the invention it all started with, while the portfolio has long since grown far beyond it.</p>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-2" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">A machine is rarely bought by one person. The engineer checks the technology, purchasing checks price and delivery capability, management checks the risk. What is bought is a technology – and the company that will still stand behind it in ten years. Products that need explaining are no disadvantage here: properly explained, they are highly desirable.</p>
  <p class="pull-quote reveal reveal-delay-2">A technical advantage only becomes a reason when someone translates what it means for each decision-maker.</p>
</section>

